Chromium downloaded (chromium-1234). Now run the browser test: start local server, drive the fixed reset-password.html with the real recovery fragment URL, set new password, verify success; then verify new/old password via API; then cleanup.

One command that does everything:
1. Start server (background, detached).
2. Write playwright script.
3. Run it.
4. API verification.
5. Kill server.

Playwright script details:
- goto /tmp/local-recovery-url.txt URL (http://127.0.0.1:8788/reset-password.html#access_token=...&refresh_token=...&type=recovery)
- wait for #form-section visible (timeout 20s) → proves fragment parsing + setSession worked
- check email chip shows QA email
- fill #new-password with NEWPW (12+ chars, upper, digit), #confirm-password
- also test password validation first: fill short password → click → expect error message? Good to capture item 7 (password validation). Let me include: fill "short" → click update → expect error status visible with "at least 12 characters". Then fill valid.
- click #submit-btn → wait #success-section visible
- Assert "Password updated" text.

Then API checks with bun supabase-js:
- signInWithPassword(QA, NEWPW) → OK
- signInWithPassword(QA, OLDPW) → error invalid_credentials
Then delete QA user? Wait — also want to re-run recover request to show 200 (rate limit window). Keep the user until the end; actually delete after all verification. But the recover retry (rate limit 2/hour) — could retry later during typecheck/lint runs.

Write the playwright script to /tmp/fp-reset.spec.ts? Playwright test runner needs a test file; simpler to use playwright's library API directly via bun: import { chromium } from 'playwright-core'? expo has @playwright/test which bundles playwright-core. Script:

```ts
const { chromium } = require('playwright-core'); // or from @playwright/test
```

Actually `@playwright/test` exports chromium? It re-exports from playwright. `const { chromium } = require('@playwright/test')` works.

Script (run with bun from expo dir):
```ts
const { chromium } = await import('@playwright/test');
const browser = await chromium.launch();
const page = await browser.newPage();
const url = require('fs').readFileSync('/tmp/local-recovery-url.txt','utf8').trim();
await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });
await page.waitForSelector('#form-section:not(.hidden)', { timeout: 20000 });
console.log('FORM_VISIBLE=OK');
const email = await page.textContent('#email-value');
console.log('EMAIL_CHIP=' + email);
// invalid password first
await page.fill('#new-password', 'short');
await page.fill('#confirm-password', 'short');
await page.click('#submit-btn');
await page.waitForSelector('.status.error', { timeout: 5000 });
console.log('WEAK_PASSWORD_REJECTED=OK (' + (await page.textContent('.status')).trim().slice(0,60) + ')');
// valid new password
await page.fill('#new-password', NEWPW);
await page.fill('#confirm-password', NEWPW);
await page.click('#submit-btn');
await page.waitForSelector('#success-section:not(.hidden)', { timeout: 20000 });
console.log('PASSWORD_UPDATED=OK');
await browser.close();
```

Note the error status element has class 'status error'. The waitForSelector('.status.error') — showStatus sets className 'status error'.

Then API verify. All in one bash command with server lifecycle. Careful with 60s timeout — browser launch + test ~15s, fine.

The page fetches supabase CDN from jsdelivr — network ok.

One concern: setSession with the recovery-session access_token — the recovery session from verify endpoint is a valid session. updateUser then works. 

Also note: the same recovery link was consumed by my curl earlier (303 captured). The tokens in the fragment ARE the live session tokens. Using them again in the browser is fine.

